---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../../components/Nav.astro';
import '../../../styles/global.css';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="About the Salido research portal — historical research on Nagari Salido, West Sumatra."
>
  <Nav lang="en" />

  <main style="padding-top: 7rem; padding-bottom: 6rem; padding-left: 2.5rem; padding-right: 2.5rem;">
    <article style="max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; font-family: var(--font-body);">

      <a
        href="/en"
        style="display: inline-block; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.9rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--color-muted); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(94,85,80,0.25); padding-bottom: 1px; margin-bottom: 3rem; transition: color 200ms, border-color 200ms;"
      >&#8592; Home</a>

      <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; color: var(--color-text);">About this Project</h1>

      <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
        This portal documents the history of Nagari Salido's gold mines on the west coast of Sumatra — a colonial experiment spanning the VOC era (1681) through the Dutch East Indies period (1881–1937). The research draws on primary sources from Nationaal Archief Den Haag and Rijksmuseum Amsterdam.
      </p>

      <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
        The project accompanies the book <em>&#8220;Sillida — Gunung Arum, The Failed Colonial Enclave&#8221;</em> (forthcoming), examining how colonial ambition collided with the realities of Minangkabau society, tropical geography, and the economics of extraction.
      </p>

      <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        The interactive atlas traces 4,700+ VOC voyages in West Sumatra, 1700–1790, providing spatial context for the trading networks that connected Salido to Padang, Pulau Cingkuak, and the wider Samudra Hindia economy.
      </p>

      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-family: var(--font-ui); color: var(--color-muted); border-top: 1px solid rgba(94,85,80,0.18); padding-top: 1.75rem; margin-top: 1rem;">
        For research inquiries &mdash; <a href="mailto:ladangminang@gmail.com" style="color: var(--color-accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(122,92,16,0.3); padding-bottom: 1px;">ladangminang@gmail.com</a>
      </p>

    </article>
  </main>

</Base>
